    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §344-d, Hway L",
    "lawSection": "Highway Law",
    "memo": "BILL NUMBER:S3468A\n\nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to amend the highway law, in relation to\ndesignating a portion of the state highway system as the \"Trooper\nChristopher G. Skinner Memorial Bridge\"\n\nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nDesignates a portion of the state highway system as the \"Trooper\nChristopher G. Skinner Memorial Bridge\".\n\nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds section 344-d to the highway law designating the\nnorthbound and southbound bridges on interstate route eighty-one\ncrossing US route eleven at exit seven, in the town of Chenango, in\nthe county of Broome, shall each be designated and known as the\n\"Trooper Christopher G. Skinner Memorial Bridge\".\n\nSection 2 states the Commissioner of Transportation shall provide for\nthe installation and maintenance of adequate signing of the \"Trooper\nChristopher G. Skinner Memorial Bridge\".\n\nSection 3 establishes the act shall take effect immediately.\n\nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nOn May 29, 2014, Trooper Christopher G. Skinner was intentionally\nstruck and killed while issuing a traffic ticket on Interstate 81\nbetween Exits 6 and 7 in the Town of Chenango, County of Broome, New\nYork. Trooper Skinner at the time of his death was assigned to the New\nYork State Police Traffic Incident Management (TIM) detail that was\ncreated to ensure the safety of the construction workers and motoring\npublic in work zones on the highways of New York.\n\nThe Work Zone Safety Act of 2005, that created the TIM detail, was\nimplemented following one of the worst work zone accidents in New York\nState history. On May 20, 2005 three highway workers were killed in a\nwork zone on Interstate 81 in the Town of Chenango when a charter bus\nstruck a tractor trailer and started a chain reaction leading to the\ndeaths. Ironically, Trooper Skinner was the first Trooper to arrive on\nthe scene of this horrific accident and became acutely aware of the\nneed for a police presence in the work zones. When the TIM detail was\nformed, he requested and was assigned to this critical function of the\nhighway safety system.\n\nIt is only proper that we forever memorialize Trooper Skinner's\ndedication to service of the people of the State of New York by\ndesignating a portion of Interstate 81 in his honor.\n\nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone.\n\nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone.\n\n\nEFFECTIVE DATE:\n\nEffective immediately.\n\n",
